 {"ts": "2026-10-11T09:08:35+00:00", "slice": "2.R", "source": "correctness", "severity": "should", "rule_id": null, "file": "src-tauri/src/window.rs", "line": 102, "problem": "There is no minimum age for \"unanswered\": a second close request 100 ms after the first destroys the window if the ping has not come back yet. A double-click on \u00d7 while the page's JS is busy (e.g. right after opening a large file) therefore closes a live page without its 'Cancel File Merge' question and loses unsaved work ([INFERENCE] on timing).", "fix": "Treat the page as gone only when the earlier request has been unanswered for at least a named `UNANSWERED_CLOSE_GRACE` (e.g. 1 s) and at most UNANSWERED_CLOSE_TIMEOUT. While it is younger than the grace, keep `since` instead of replacing it. Add boundary tests at the grace and at grace \u2212 1 ms."}
